{number: 127}
{title: I Am Coming, Lord}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] I hear Thy welcome voice,
That calls me, [Bb7] Lord, to [Eb] Thee
For cleansing in Thy [Ab] precious blood
That [Eb] flowed on [Bb7] Calva-[Eb] ry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb] I am coming, Lord!
[Bb7] Coming now to [Eb] Thee!
Wash me, cleanse me in the [Ab] blood
That [Eb] flowed on [Bb7] Calva-[Eb] ry!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Tho' [Eb] coming weak and vile,
Thou dost my [Bb7] strength as-[Eb] sure;
Thou dost my vileness [Ab] fully cleanse,
Till [Eb] spotless [Bb7] all and [Eb] pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
'Tis [Eb] Jesus calls me on
To perfect [Bb7] faith and [Eb] love,
To perfect hope, and [Ab] peace, and trust,
For [Eb] earth and [Bb7] heav'n a-[Eb] bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
'Tis [Eb] Jesus who confirms
The blessed [Bb7] work with-[Eb] in,
By adding grace to [Ab] welcomed grace,
Where [Eb] reigned the [Bb7] pow'r of [Eb] sin.
{end_of_verse}
